{"created": "2024-01-22T09:45:18.590067+00:00", "modified": "2024-01-22T09:45:18.714594+00:00", "id": 10539202, "conceptrecid": "10034611", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10539202", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.10034611", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10539202", "metadata": {"title": "GitBug-Actions Go Benchmark January 2023", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10539202", "publication_date": "2024-01-20", "description": "<p>The files are organized as follows:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>collect_repos\n<ul>\n<li>Contains the execution files of the scanned repositories (one file per repo, with execution results)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>collect_bugs&nbsp;\n<ul>\n<li>Contains files generated by the \"collect_bugs\" step, which include all identifed bug-fix commits (one file per repo, one line per bug-fix commit).</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>export_bugs <br>\n<ul>\n<li>Contains files generated by executing&nbsp; GHAs locally for each bug-fix commit. Required for offline execution.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>filter_repos\n<ul>\n<li>Contains the list of bug-fix commits considered as flaky, non-flaky, and high-quality.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>repos\n<ul>\n<li>Contains the cloned repositories from which the non-flaky bug-fix commits were collected.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Saavedra, Nuno", "affiliation": "Instituto de Engenharia de Sistemas e Computadores Investiga\u00e7\u00e3o e Desenvolvimento", "orcid": "0000-0003-4148-5991"}, {"name": "Silva, Andr\u00e9", "affiliation": "KTH Royal Institute of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0001-6667-4970"}, {"name": "Monperrus, Martin", "affiliation": "KTH Royal Institute of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0003-3505-3383"}], "dates": [{"type": "accepted"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "alternate_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/gitbugactions/gitbugactions"}], "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 3, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "reci